{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLrqjRqJz1caZF2GXkGq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it. All four methods named in the issue (`is_parallel`, `is_perpendicular`, `angle_between` and `smallest_angle_between`) now raise `TypeError: Must pass only LinearEntity objects` when given a non-line argument like a `Point`.\n\nThe cause was a wrong condition in the type check in `sympy/geometry/line.py`. It used `and` where it needed `or`, so the error only fired when *both* arguments were invalid. With one valid line and one `Point`, the check passed and the code then crashed trying to read `.direction` from the `Point`. I changed `and` to `or` in all four places; nothing else in the file changed.\n\nI ran the issue's example against all four methods and each raised the `TypeError`. The existing tests in `sympy/geometry/tests/test_line.py` all pass (36 tests)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":571,"cache_read_input_tokens":18865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":571},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6d795cf-01fc-4157-9d68-01c7da6ef66b","uuid":"7392e928-ee59-4ff5-a71b-645739c1e465","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:09:17.175Z","request_id":"req_011ChLrqjJeGqgY9keNsH1Wa"}
